{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Come on in, love. I did his blood pressure out there, one thirty two over eighty six, heart rate eighty eight beats a minute, and the oxygen saturations were ninety eight percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks, Niamh. Sorry, this yoke is frozen again. Sit down there.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): It's the cough, doctor. That's why I brought him.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. How long is the cough going?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two weeks, well, actually a few weeks. I couldn't tell you the day. I put it down to a cold.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the screen jumped. A few weeks, did you say?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): A few weeks, yeah. It started like a cold and the cough just stayed.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sean, you coughing?",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is it a dry cough or a wet one?",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (PATIENT): Dry.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Bone dry, no phlegm at all. And it's worse at night, I'd say.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any temperature with it at home?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No fever.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is he short of breath, running around the yard?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand, I'll not write that down as a yes. Now, the pressure. He's on enalapril?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He is. For the high blood pressure. Five milligrams, once a day, about a month now.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Give me that dose again, I typed two point five by mistake.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Five. The five milligram ones. Every morning with his breakfast.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Five milligrams, once daily, yes, that's what's on the chart. Is he getting every dose?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He is. I don't miss them.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Anything else he's taking?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Nothing of his own. My father takes lisinopril, and the chemist said it's the same sort of tablet, so I wondered.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): That's your father's, not Sean's. We won't put lisinopril on his list.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (NURSE): I never got a temperature. Will I do it now?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Please.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (NURSE): Thirty six point seven celsius.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any wheeze? Any pain in the chest?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No wheeze, and no chest pain.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies? Penicillin or anything?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say it again, someone was talking in the corridor.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No allergies.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Was the traffic desperate getting in?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ah, the M50 was at a standstill. Rain belting down the whole way. My sister's lad had his hurling match called off yesterday, the pitch was underwater.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): They'd have been skating, not hurling. More rain till Thursday, apparently.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): So the radio said. And I left the dog shut in the kitchen, he'll have the place destroyed.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ha, right, back to Sean. Enalapril is an ACE inhibitor, and they can cause a dry cough. It might be the tablet, or it might be the tail of that cold. I'm not making a diagnosis of the cough today.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): So it could be either.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): Either. What I'll do is stop the enalapril from today and change him to amlodipine, two point five milligrams, once every morning.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Stop the old one completely?",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Completely. No more of the enalapril five milligrams once a day that he started about a month ago for his blood pressure. The amlodipine is two point five milligrams by mouth, once a day, for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Will the cough stop straight away?",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (DOCTOR): It can hang on a few weeks after the tablet is stopped, so don't panic if it's still there.",
  "[SEG0048] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And if it isn't gone?",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (DOCTOR): If it's no better in a fortnight, we might do a chest x-ray. I'm not booking one now.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll see him back here in two weeks to check the pressure on the new tablet.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (NURSE): I'll book the two weeks at reception on the way out.",
  "[SEG0052] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Does he stay off school?",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (DOCTOR): No, send him in. Plenty of drinks, and I'd leave the cough bottles. I wouldn't give him one.",
  "[SEG0054] person_4 (PATIENT): School?",
  "[SEG0055] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): You're grand for school.",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (DOCTOR): Headaches? Or is he otherwise himself?",
  "[SEG0057] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No headaches. He's himself.",
  "[SEG0058] person_4 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0059] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lovely. The prescription will be waiting at the desk. That's us.",
  "[SEG0060] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Thanks a million.",
  "[SEG0061] person_1 (NURSE): Come on, ye, we'll sort the appointment."
 ],
